sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant S as Source
    participant A as Host 1
    participant B as Host 2
    participant C as Host 3
    Note over S,C: naive: the source sends the file 1000 times and its NIC is the wall
    S->>A: chunk 1
    A->>B: chunk 1, while receiving chunk 2
    S->>A: chunk 2
    B->>C: chunk 1
    A->>B: chunk 2
    Note over S,C: a pipelined chain — total time approaches one transfer plus the chain depth
    par or a tree
        A->>B: fan out
        A->>C: fan out
    end
    Note over A,C: chain gives best throughput, tree gives lowest depth — pick by link speed and host count
